/-!
# Generation of the binary derived symplectic four-group

The three commutators from `Generators` generate the actual derived subgroup
of `Sp₄(2)`. A finite certificate lists 360 matrices, each obtained from an
earlier matrix by multiplying by one of the three generators. A second
certificate covers every symplectic matrix by this list and its translate by
one fixed transvection. Thus any subgroup containing the generators has index
dividing two and contains the commutator subgroup. Applying this to the image
of the closure inside the derived group proves generation.

The integer tables are untrusted search output: all matrix identities and the
exhaustive row-pairing certificate are checked by Lean's kernel. No cardinality
assumption or identification with the full symplectic group is used.

Reference: Aschbacher--Smith, *The Classification of Quasithin Groups*,
Lemma I.1.6(5), printed p.408 (PDF p.419).
-/

